	(text "Wiring between bought boards; only the pads in use are drawn. USB-C on A1 is the charging port.\nAlways take power from the TP4056 OUT pads, not B+/B-, or the protection does nothing.\nD4 HIGH = driver on, LOW = ~1 uA sleep. The XIAO's own USB-C is for flashing only, never with the battery connected.\nESP32-H2 build: same connections on GPIO 1 (battery), 2, 3 (IN1, IN2) and 4 (nSLEEP).\nNot built or tested on hardware yet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
